  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "A researcher named Chris Ramsay, a guest on Jesse Michels' podcast, talks about Stargate, a US government programme from the 1970s to 1995 that tried to use \"remote viewing,\" the idea that a person can sense faraway places with the mind alone. Ramsay says Edwin May, the programme's chief research physicist, had to put together a scientific oversight committee to check the work, and he names figures such as Daryl Bem, Schwartz and Zimbardo in connection with it. For Ramsay, this would mean the programme was held to outside scientific scrutiny."
